&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50127187</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:08:03 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Twain, a diff viewer like Meld, but for the age of AI</title><link>https://github.com/andunieee/twain</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I love Meld, I've been using it for a while now, it's amazing how many diff viewers exist these days and how they are all awful compared to Meld.&lt;p&gt;But Meld was missing some features that I thought were worth having:&lt;p&gt;- all files from a Git diff shown in the same view, sequentially + a file tree on the side.
- show either the full files or only the parts that changed.
- tree-sitter-based syntax highlighting.
- the ability to comment on sets of changes and lines, and AIs can read these comments.
- the ability to search through the entire set of modified files.&lt;p&gt;Twain is in Rust and based on GTK4.&lt;/p&gt;
